=== REASON (NOT a regression; NOT an ADR-041 issue) ===
The dry-run smoke opens a vkms DRM card (find_vkms_card → /dev/dri/card0,
driver=vkms) and calls acquire_master_lock(). On this bench Hyprland +
systemd-logind ALREADY HOLD DRM master on card0 (vkms):

$ sudo cat /sys/kernel/debug/dri/0/clients
             command  tgid dev master a   uid      magic  name  id
      systemd-logind   476   0   y    y     0          0  ...  43
            Hyprland  1678   0   y    y  1000          0  ...  51
            Hyprland  1678   0   n    n  1000          0  ...  57

acquire_master_lock() on an already-mastered card returns EACCES/EPERM
(Permission denied, os error 13). This is the SAME documented
environmental constraint recorded in QA v5-5 (line 183-185) and v6-5
(line 376-377, 636-643): "the 3 master-gated tests CANNOT execute here
(Hyprland holds vkms master)".

=== W13 adjudication ===
The W13 task asks: does the SIM path still identify/enumerate its uinput
digitizer under the new predicate? ANSWER: the SIM path does NOT run the
structural predicate AT ALL — by design. SimInputProvider::new
(src/providers/sim_input.rs:103-105) creates its own uinput device and
matches it by evdev path (dev_node == my_path) in poll()
(sim_input.rs:255-260), NOT via is_touchbar_digitizer. The ADR-041
equivalence claim (single source of truth) is scoped to the REAL
identification path (runtime identify_digitizer + --probe-input), NOT the
sim. The sim's uinput device has vendor=0x1209/product=0x316E (NOT
05ac:8600), so even if the predicate ran on it, the iBridge-association
clause would REJECT it — but the predicate never runs on the sim path.
The ADR itself acknowledges this (line 20: "the sim, which bypasses the
gate"; line 107: "the ADR-024 scale test exercises the scale, not the
gate"). No REGRESSION: the sim path is unchanged by ADR-041.

The dry-run smoke CANNOT be executed in this bench class without
violating HOST SAFETY RULES (stopping Hyprland to free vkms master would
be a service lifecycle action on a non-oracle service the interlock does
not cover). Per ADR-026 exclusivity + the v5-5/v6-5 precedent, this is
recorded as CANNOT-EXECUTE-HERE, not a defect. The render/tap/SIGTERM
sub-checks are NOT reachable (the dry-run fails at display acquire before
input init). The cargo test suite DOES exercise the sim path (70 unit
tests pass, including test_sim_input_creates_uinput_device +
test_sim_input_scales_real_abs_range_to_logical — both green), confirming
the sim path itself is functional where master is available.